{"parentUuid":"6e67c749-3889-4996-9d38-7fc82613e101","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a21c8156ce15501b0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017AzcFHZNcQwZiddG1vsFvQ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Laurent Perron CP-SAT performance tuning 2025 site:github.com/google/or-tools\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CP-SAT get's stuck when trying to maximize sum of boolean variables that are all added as assumptions · google/or-tools · Discussion #3630\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3630\"},{\"title\":\"CP Sat is not optimizing my cost function · google/or-tools · Discussion #2491\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/2491\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT: Performance drops from 60s to 700s - why? · Issue #1102 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1102\"},{\"title\":\"Bottlenecks in CP-SAT Solver Performance Across Core Configurations · Issue #4783 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/4783\"},{\"title\":\"Cut generators in CPModelProto · Issue #912 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/912\"},{\"title\":\"Next major release will be 10.0 · google/or-tools · Discussion #3992\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3992\"},{\"title\":\"Multi-objective optimization with CP-Sat · Issue #1344 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1344\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT LNS threads · Issue #1314 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1314\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT produces nondeterministic results · Issue #3590 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3590\"}]\n\nI've completed the web search with the query you specified. The search results show several GitHub discussions and issues related to Laurent Perron, CP-SAT, and performance topics on the google/or-tools repository, though they're from various dates rather than specifically focused on 2025 performance tuning.\n\nHere's what the search found:\n\n**Key Results:**\n\n1. **Worker Configuration**: The solver is designed to work with 8+ workers, unless for trivial models, according to Laurent Perron's comments.\n\n2. **Recent Performance Issues**: A September 2025 issue discusses CP-SAT performance with different core configurations and mentions the solver's inherent randomness.\n\n3. **Solver Parameters**: The search found the sat_parameters.proto file which contains recent updates from December 2025 with new parameters for proof checking and SAT-specific features.\n\n4. **Parallelization Insights**: The solver allows specification of parallel workers to use during search, with a value of 0 meaning the solver will try to use all cores on the machine, and a value of 1 meaning no parallelism.\n\nThe results primarily show discussion threads and issues from the OR-Tools repository where Laurent Perron has provided guidance on performance optimization, particularly regarding worker/thread configuration as a key performance tuning parameter.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"f344aaaa-1063-4aea-957c-42b984ab8061","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:50:18.166Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6e67c749-3889-4996-9d38-7fc82613e101","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"9d36ffd4-adab-4a6e-ad5f-e56e1c331605","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a21c8156ce15501b0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NYjKJ7KtakbWMceKpjrrPy","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT slow large model timeout Laurent Perron suggest parameters site:groups.google.com or-tools-discuss\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Expected time to evaluate model (feasibility)\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/acul1GgXqf8\"},{\"title\":\"trying to solve huge mode on CP-Sat\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/VjiSYjFFB_4\"},{\"title\":\"Find many CP-SAT solutions, multi-threaded, under time constraint\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/GNgvcMpEwmE\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools-discuss - Google Groups\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT claims to find optimal solution to a MILP\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/4fcAuWiIUFA\"},{\"title\":\"[CP-SAT] Ortools stops when solving a RCPSP - Memory exhausted?\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/d-3P1dq-RBY\"},{\"title\":\"Monitor search in CP-SAT solver\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/r54A2eokoXk\"},{\"title\":\"Solving time\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/Ui6VVTiBs28\"},{\"title\":\"Parallel search problem in CP-SAT solver\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/i3TF_Szuz_k\"},{\"title\":\"Seeding CP-SAT solver\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/lPb1FzhTMt0\"}]\n\nI found several relevant discussions from the or-tools-discuss Google Group. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Relevant Discussion: CP-SAT with Large Models and Timeouts\n\nA user reported running the CP-SAT solver on a large bin-packing-like problem with O(7M) variables and O(30M) constraints, which took almost 10 hours just to verify an initial solution using solution_hint.\n\n### Parameter Suggestions from Laurent Perron\n\nOne suggestion was to try the parameter `--params linearization_level:0` since the LP might be taking time.\n\n### Additional Performance Tuning Options\n\nFor handling large models with timeouts, the search results show other parameter configurations:\n\n- Parameters like `log_search_progress: true`, `cp_model_presolve: false`, `linearization_level: 0`, and `num_workers: 1` were used in testing\n- Setting `max_time_in_seconds` and `num_search_workers` to control solver behavior\n\nThe discussions indicate that when CP-SAT becomes slow with large models, adjusting presolve settings and linearization levels can help address performance issues, though the optimal parameters depend heavily on the specific model characteristics.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"a39a70b0-1a4e-4da1-aec6-29f249accea9","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:50:20.021Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9d36ffd4-adab-4a6e-ad5f-e56e1c331605","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"0d697718-2bf1-49f3-9208-2e8d43a71841","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a21c8156ce15501b0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ErdudrCqVpZieHZYr9wqEe","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools CP-SAT num_workers num_search_workers Laurent Perron recommendation 2024 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Parallel search problem in CP-SAT solver\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/i3TF_Szuz_k\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Laurent Perron\",\"url\":\"https://research.google/people/105821/\"},{\"title\":\"dblp: Laurent Perron\",\"url\":\"https://dblp.org/pid/73/4963.html\"},{\"title\":\"Laurent PERRON | Tech Lead Operations Research | PhD Computer Science | Google Inc., Mountain View | Google | Research Department | Research profile\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Laurent-Perron-2\"},{\"title\":\"The CP-SAT-LP Solver (Invited Talk) - DROPS\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2023.3\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT solver couldn't prove the solution is optimal if num_workers < 5 but otherwise it did instantly. · Issue #3662 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3662\"},{\"title\":\"Monitor search in CP-SAT solver\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/r54A2eokoXk\"},{\"title\":\"Laurent Perron\",\"url\":\"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=umrglaIAAAAJ&hl=en\"},{\"title\":\"The CP-SAT-LP Solver Laurent Perron # Google, Paris, France Frédéric Didier #\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol280-cp2023/LIPIcs.CP.2023.3/LIPIcs.CP.2023.3.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about Laurent Perron and CP-SAT parallelization work. Let me provide you with what I found:\n\nLaurent Perron's recent work investigates the effectiveness of splitting the search space in parallelizing the CP-SAT solver, noting that one of the key barriers to effective search-space splitting in learning solvers is that generated sub-problems are not independent, leading to substantial communication-related overhead and redundant work.\n\nHis contributions attempt to mitigate this issue through job reassignment and trail sharing, where jobs (sub-trees) are reassigned to new workers if the clause database of the currently assigned worker appears ill-suited to the region of the search-space, and workers can share some of the state from their local trail.\n\nThese approaches complement standard portfolio and clause-sharing approaches, improving CP-SAT's performance on MiniZinc challenge benchmarks with a moderate number of worker threads, and introduce \"Buffered Work Stealing,\" which can be parameterized to emulate the two main existing approaches to search-space splitting in the literature: Work Stealing and Embarrassingly Parallel Search, as well as an intermediate configuration between these two extremes.\n\nThe search results also show that CP-SAT-LP implements and relies upon a portfolio of diverse workers for its search part.\n\nHowever, I did not find specific recommendations about the `num_workers` and `num_search_workers` parameters from Laurent Perron in the 2024-2025 timeframe in these search results. For more specific parameter tuning recommendations, you may want to check the official OR-Tools documentation or recent GitHub discussions.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"cbe3959d-d7d9-448a-bd08-df39cfd16798","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:50:20.357Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0d697718-2bf1-49f3-9208-2e8d43a71841","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
