{"parentUuid":"5b30d678-6008-4967-b017-a1ed4a5d018a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a21c8156ce15501b0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X6HGskpMTbpNA3AN9FbfTp","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT Primer d-krupke parameters recommendations 2025 lperron interesting subsolver\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding the Log - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/understanding_the_log.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"cpsat-primer/understanding_the_log.md at main · d-krupke/cpsat-primer\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer/blob/main/understanding_the_log.md\"},{\"title\":\"cpsat-primer/README.md at main · d-krupke/cpsat-primer\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer/blob/main/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"Large Neighborhood Search - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/09_lns.html\"},{\"title\":\"cpsat-primer/evaluations/packing/solver/knapsack_wo_rotations.py at main · d-krupke/cpsat-primer\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer/blob/main/evaluations/packing/solver/knapsack_wo_rotations.py\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://github-com.translate.goog/d-krupke/cpsat-primer?_x_tr_sl=en&_x_tr_tl=es&_x_tr_hl=es&_x_tr_pto=tc\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about the CP-SAT Primer by Dominik Krupke (d-krupke) which covers parameters and subsolver configurations. Here's what I found:\n\n## Parameters and Subsolver Recommendations\n\nWith a single worker, only the default subsolver is used. With two workers or more, CP-SAT starts using incomplete subsolvers, i.e., heuristics such as LNS. With five workers, CP-SAT will also have a first solution subsolver. With 32 workers, all 15 full problem subsolvers are used. For more than 32 workers, primarily the number of first solution subsolvers is increased.\n\n## Important Configuration Guidance\n\nIt is important not to modify the parameters at the top level, as this would affect all subsolvers, including the LNS-workers. Doing so could disrupt the balance of the portfolio, potentially activating costly techniques for the LNS-workers, which could slow them down to the point of being ineffective. Additionally, you risk creating a default subsolver incompatible with your model - such as one that requires an objective function - causing CP-SAT to exclude most or all subsolvers from the portfolio.\n\n## Parameter Tuning Considerations\n\nBased on this data, you could try to tune the various parameters of CP-SAT for your problem. However, note that you will probably need a lot of experience and experiments to gain an advantage compared to the default settings.\n\nThe search results provide practical guidance from the CP-SAT Primer, though they don't include specific 2025 recommendations or references to \"lperron\" (Laurent Perron, a key CP-SAT developer). For more detailed parameter recommendations, you may want to consult the full CP-SAT Primer at https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/ or the official Google OR-Tools documentation.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"54be5f20-bd05-4dbc-8637-643557213418","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:50:38.625Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5b30d678-6008-4967-b017-a1ed4a5d018a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a17ccbb6-c547-43a2-a029-ff059e797f23","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a21c8156ce15501b0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FmohUxUnpgbLx7f7PLaWCg","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"lperron\" CP-SAT placement packing 2D performance hint github issue\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"lperron (Laurent Perron) · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/lperron\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding performance loss of solving my model with SatSolver in comparison to CspSolver · Issue #1028 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1028\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - johnMinelli/CP-SAT-SMT_2D-StripPacking: 2D Strip Packing problem solved with different approaches\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/johnMinelli/CP-SAT-SMT_2D-StripPacking\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT: performance tips for the enumeration of all solutions · google/or-tools · Discussion #4223\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/4223\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ktnr/BinPacking2D: Exact solutions for two-dimensional bin packing problems by branch-and-cut · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ktnr/BinPacking2D\"},{\"title\":\"Difference between constraint solver's LNS with CP-SAT's LNS? · google/or-tools · Discussion #2829\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/2829\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"Performance of packing problems · google/or-tools · Discussion #3177\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3177\"},{\"title\":\"Advanced Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04B_advanced_modelling.html\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found relevant information related to your query about CP-SAT, 2D packing, performance, and hints:\n\nFor packing problems, certain expensive propagation techniques can significantly speed up the search but can also drastically slow it down if misused. To handle this, you can add a single subsolver that applies these techniques.\n\nFor packing subsolvers, parameters like `use_area_energetic_reasoning_in_no_overlap_2d`, `use_energetic_reasoning_in_no_overlap_2d`, `use_timetabling_in_no_overlap_2d`, and `max_pairs_pairwise_reasoning_in_no_overlap_2d` can be configured.\n\nRegarding performance hints: If you have a good intuition about how the solution might look, you can inform CP-SAT to incorporate this knowledge into its search. Some workers will try to follow these hints, which can significantly improve the solver's performance if they are good. If the hints actually represent a feasible solution, the solver can use them to prune the search space of all branches that have worse bounds than the hints.\n\nAdditionally, considerable performance improvements for 2D packing problems have been observed since version 9.2. The parameter `use_energetic_reasoning_in_no_overlap_2d` is available and `use_cumulative_in_no_overlap_2d` has been renamed to `use_timetabling_in_no_overlap_2d`.\n\nThe search results reference GitHub discussions related to these topics, particularly discussion #3177 which focuses on performance of packing problems.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"5d7e8c3a-6f07-429e-83ff-fd895f7f4920","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:50:38.694Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a17ccbb6-c547-43a2-a029-ff059e797f23","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"ce41d474-cf3f-4916-a5f7-ff552ec1d5bb","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a21c8156ce15501b0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TDzG4kwcagsyXD9iGm3p7e","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools 9.12 9.13 9.14 9.15 release notes changelog CP-SAT performance\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Release Notes | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/support/release_notes\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/releases\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/docs/README.md at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/docs/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"ortools · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/ortools/\"},{\"title\":\"Changelog vs. release notes: What’s the difference and when to use each\",\"url\":\"https://www.appcues.com/blog/changelog-vs-release-notes\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT, UNKNOWN status with complete solution hint · Issue #3750 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3750\"},{\"title\":\"Releases - Apple Developer\",\"url\":\"https://developer.apple.com/news/releases/\"},{\"title\":\"Top 10 Changelog & Release Notes Tools: Features, Pros, Cons & Comparison -\",\"url\":\"https://www.devopsschool.com/blog/top-10-changelog-release-notes-tools-features-pros-cons-comparison/\"},{\"title\":\"Red Hat Satellite Release Dates - Red Hat Customer Portal\",\"url\":\"https://access.redhat.com/articles/1365633\"},{\"title\":\"Release Notes vs Changelog: Understanding the Key Differences and When to Use Each | LaunchNotes\",\"url\":\"https://www.launchnotes.com/blog/release-notes-vs-changelog-understanding-the-key-differences-and-when-to-use-each\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about OR-Tools versions 9.12, 9.13, 9.14, and 9.15 release notes:\n\n## OR-Tools Release Versions\n\nOR-Tools has released versions 9.15, 9.14, 9.13, and 9.12.\n\n## CP-SAT Improvements\n\nThe search results show several CP-SAT and performance-related improvements across these versions:\n\n- Fix CP-SAT logging callback crash when using multiple workers\n- Improve robustness of the LNS code, improve scheduling code with new factory methods to create fixed size intervals, new search heuristics, improved presolve and new linear cuts, and improve routing code with new dedicated LNS\n- Improve MIP code with better presolve and multiple improvements to the linear relaxation of MIP and CP models, improve search diversity, and when using more than 12 workers, add workers dedicated to improving the lower bound of the objective\n- CP-SAT callbacks in Python, Java, .NET can slow down search performance\n\nFor more detailed information about specific changes in each version, you can visit the official OR-Tools Release Notes on Google for Developers or the GitHub Releases page for OR-Tools.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"55ec85e0-4185-41d3-8811-7fdcbd169fe3","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:50:38.952Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ce41d474-cf3f-4916-a5f7-ff552ec1d5bb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"37230f62-ca10-4d78-9f57-b84f4b8e727e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a21c8156ce15501b0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W1Tvan9z5pv9QJz8ULhn6i","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP-SAT Parameter Recommendations Analysis\n\nBased on the provided web page content, I found **no specific parameter recommendations from Laurent Perron or Frédéric Didier**. The document does not attribute any recommendations to these individuals by name.\n\n## General Parameter Recommendations Found\n\nThe page provides recommendations from the unnamed author (Dominik Krupke), including:\n\n- **`max_time_in_seconds`**: Set between 60-300 seconds as a starting point for time-limited solving\n- **`log_search_progress = True`**: Enable during development to understand solver behavior\n- **`relative_gap_limit = 0.05`**: Stop when solution is provably within 5% of optimum\n- **`num_workers`**: Reduce to match physical cores (not hyperthreads) for potential performance gains\n- **`fix_variables_to_their_hinted_value = True`**: Verify hint feasibility\n- **`cp_model_presolve = False`**: Disable only if presolve dominates runtime on simple models\n\n## Recent Updates/New Features\n\nThe document mentions **CP-SAT version 9.10** and describes:\n- Bound callbacks (newly supported feature)\n- Export/import functionality for model comparison across hardware\n- Enhanced hint preservation mechanisms\n\n**No 2024-2026 updates or new subsolvers are mentioned** in this content."}]},"uuid":"81bc9ffa-2d95-468d-93bb-e7a427c97d62","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:50:39.887Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"37230f62-ca10-4d78-9f57-b84f4b8e727e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
