{"parentUuid":"3b8450be-ba00-4f7d-960a-b54202f8f235","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a21c8156ce15501b0","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01DDs4jxcjf4vmfvZXHV8Svs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014zv1LuwsCot6xRnyd8Ks9V","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"\"linearization_level\" CP-SAT \"2\" OR \"3\" Laurent Perron recommendation packing"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4876,"cache_read_input_tokens":27485,"output_tokens":560,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4876},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":560,"cache_read_input_tokens":27485,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4876,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4876,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaosMH4Dob8Ug6x5SrigM","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"0e068d20-d859-4ad0-b22a-9d78a06d44da","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:50:46.673Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"6894c79e-f45b-4db2-b229-caa0ace960f6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a21c8156ce15501b0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TyEfhayrSo6E3frAXpyAk5","type":"tool_result","content":"# Laurent Perron's Responses on CP-SAT Performance\n\nBased on the provided web page content, **there are no responses from Laurent Perron visible**. \n\nThe page shows:\n- An issue opened by Cheah-ds on September 9, 2025\n- The issue is assigned to lperron (Laurent Perron)\n- The issue describes concerns about CP-SAT randomness and performance degradation with `interleave_search=True`\n\nHowever, the actual discussion thread, comments, or any responses from Laurent Perron are not included in the content provided. To access his specific parameter recommendations and reasoning, you would need to view the full issue discussion thread on GitHub."}]},"uuid":"da740e86-3468-4f66-a659-562db433ba68","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:50:47.744Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6894c79e-f45b-4db2-b229-caa0ace960f6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"9036f60b-e635-4700-af96-70105e49c4cc","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a21c8156ce15501b0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HGBhnvF5JEGeNuhjvJVpvR","type":"tool_result","content":"# Laurent Perron's Parameter Recommendations for 2D Packing\n\nBased on the discussion thread, Laurent Perron (the maintainer) made **no explicit parameter recommendations** for improving 2D packing performance.\n\n## What Perron Actually Said\n\nWhen asked about performance differences, Perron's only substantive comment was:\n\n> \"Actually, the no_overlap_2d propagator is poor. I want to implement stronger versions, but I lack the time to do that.\"\n\nThis indicates a limitation in the existing propagator rather than suggesting parameter adjustments to users.\n\n## What Perron Asked Instead\n\nRather than recommending specific parameters, Perron asked clarifying questions:\n- Whether the user was running with multiple workers\n- Whether they could test with 16 workers if hardware permitted\n\nPerron then reported his own benchmark results (70s and 630s on his 2018 workstation with 16 workers and default settings) but did not translate these into parameter guidance for users.\n\n## Conclusion\n\nThe discussion shows Perron acknowledging the performance gap but deferring solutions to future development work rather than offering parameter tuning advice."}]},"uuid":"13778464-fb6b-4346-80ed-ff56bac54f7d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:50:48.545Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9036f60b-e635-4700-af96-70105e49c4cc","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"0e068d20-d859-4ad0-b22a-9d78a06d44da","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a21c8156ce15501b0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014zv1LuwsCot6xRnyd8Ks9V","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"linearization_level\" CP-SAT \"2\" OR \"3\" Laurent Perron recommendation packing\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CP-SAT for scheduling Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://schedulingseminar.com/presentations/SchedulingSeminar_LaurentPerron.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Expected time to evaluate model (feasibility)\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/acul1GgXqf8\"},{\"title\":\"[Scheduling seminar] Laurent Perron (Google France) | The CP-SAT solver - YouTube\",\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vvUxusrUcpU\"},{\"title\":\"dblp: Laurent Perron\",\"url\":\"https://dblp.org/pid/73/4963.html\"},{\"title\":\"Monitor search in CP-SAT solver\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/r54A2eokoXk\"},{\"title\":\"The CP-SAT-LP Solver Laurent Perron # Google, Paris, France Frédéric Didier #\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol280-cp2023/LIPIcs.CP.2023.3/LIPIcs.CP.2023.3.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"lperron (Laurent Perron) · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/lperron\"},{\"title\":\"ViolationLS: Constraint-Based Local Search in CP-SAT | Integration of Constraint Programming, Artificial Intelligence, and Operations Research\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1007/978-3-031-60597-0_16\"},{\"title\":\"CPMpy ortools interface (cpmpy.solvers.ortools) — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/solve_status/api/solvers/ortools.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about the `linearization_level` parameter in CP-SAT:\n\nThe `linearization_level` parameter in CP-SAT has a default value of 1 and can be set to 0, 2, or potentially other values. \n\nIn the context of a bin-packing problem discussion, Laurent Perron recommended trying `--params linearization_level:0` since the LP might be the one taking time. This suggestion was made when dealing with performance issues on large problems.\n\nAdditionally, the linearization_level flag was noted as a configuration difference that could affect performance, and it was suggested to launch jobs on full models with linearization_level=0.\n\nThe documentation also indicates that linearization_level=0 disables linearization (default: 1, can also set to 2).\n\nHowever, the search results don't explicitly contain Laurent Perron's specific recommendation for which level (2 or 3) to use for packing problems, though the discussion does show that adjusting this parameter can significantly impact solver performance.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"5aca1c2d-7ec2-4c2e-a3a4-cbf6b859eb35","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:50:52.124Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0e068d20-d859-4ad0-b22a-9d78a06d44da","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"3b8450be-ba00-4f7d-960a-b54202f8f235","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a21c8156ce15501b0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ABaRc3gEB1ZP4ycP8SrCEL","type":"tool_result","content":"# OR-Tools Release Notes: Versions 9.12-9.15+\n\n## Version 9.15 (January 2026)\n\n**CP-SAT Enhancements:**\n- Support for set variables and constraints (experimental)\n- Extended enforcement literal support across more constraints\n- Improved linear1 and linear2 encodings\n- Enhanced shared tree workers and clause sharing\n- Extensive LRAT proof production and checking work\n\n**Packing & Scheduling:**\n- Significant improvements to `no_overlap_2d` constraint covering \"presolve, propagation, and cuts\"\n- Precedence detection and utilization in presolve, propagation, and cuts\n- Improved scheduling cuts and memory management\n\n**Python & Performance:**\n- Optimized Python layer and proto generation\n- Enhanced gil-less Python 3.14 support\n- Multiple bug fixes and heuristic improvements\n\n**Dependencies:** HiGHS v1.12.0, SCIP v10.0.0, Protobuf v33.1\n\n---\n\n## Version 9.13 (June 2024)\n\n**CP-SAT Improvements:**\n- Enhancements to `no_overlap_2d` constraint including \"presolve, propagation, and cuts\"\n- Precedence detection with bounds (lb ≤ ax + by ≤ ub) integrated into presolve and propagation\n- Routing cuts deepened to detect node transitions and capacity constraints\n- Improved clause sharing between portfolio search workers\n\n**Dependencies:** abseil-cpp 20250512.0, Protobuf v31.0, HiGHS v1.10.0, SCIP v922\n\n---\n\n## Version 9.12 (February 2025)\n\n**CP-SAT Features:**\n- RandomHalfBranching search heuristics added\n- Improved cumulative propagation and cuts\n- Hint transformation rewrite during presolve preserving feasible solutions\n- 1-variable affine expression support in Automaton and Element constraints\n- LNS speedup and numerous fuzzer-discovered bug fixes\n\n**Packing & Scheduling:**\n- Enhanced `no_overlap_2d` layer improvements\n- Scheduling samples added\n- Job affinity implementation with shared tree workers\n\n**Dependencies:** Protobuf 29.3, HiGHS 1.9.0, SCIP v920\n\n---\n\n## Version 9.14 (June 2024)\n\n**Minor Release Notes:**\n- CFT heuristic for set covering introduced\n- Set-cover outer refinement procedure implemented\n- MacOS libscip linkage issue resolved\n\n**Dependencies:** Protobuf v31.1\n\n---\n\n## Summary of Key Trends\n\nAcross these versions, OR-Tools demonstrates consistent focus on constraint propagation efficiency, particularly for packing problems via `no_overlap_2d` improvements. Python performance optimization and support for newer Python versions (3.13-3.14) remain priorities, alongside experimental features like set variables and enhanced proof generation for constraint satisfaction problems."}]},"uuid":"ecb283ff-1a42-4d43-bcfc-7b8dadace843","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:50:56.617Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3b8450be-ba00-4f7d-960a-b54202f8f235","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
