{"parentUuid":"4586d40f-cafa-48a2-b9e9-f685d7010de8","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a21c8156ce15501b0","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01NED9njzwHcBEJGcV6Z3cxm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XKZoE6AxozWCdRw1MAZyx9","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/VjiSYjFFB_4","prompt":"Extract Laurent Perron's specific advice for solving huge CP-SAT models. Include exact parameter recommendations, his explanations, and direct quotes."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1146,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2233,"cache_read_input_tokens":32361,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2233,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":51,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaosNWcaHBKTmgYzK351i","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"7c5eabe9-c54e-4abc-b1a3-2a5ad111da2e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:02.542Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"4586d40f-cafa-48a2-b9e9-f685d7010de8","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a21c8156ce15501b0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RFiA4YEuH2fqyu5QRoswfK","type":"tool_result","content":"# Laurent Perron's Performance Recommendation\n\nBased on the GitHub discussion, Laurent Perron (OR-Tools maintainer) provided this specific recommendation for enumerating all solutions:\n\n**\"Look for embarrassingly parallel search. Basically select k variables, create all possible assignments, enumerate all solutions from one possible assignment in parallel. Bonus point if you only generate valid assignments.\"**\n\n## Parameter Configuration\n\nThe discussion shows the user already implementing the relevant parameter:\n\n```python\nself._solver.parameters.enumerate_all_solutions = all_solutions\n```\n\nHowever, Perron's response notably **does not specify additional solver parameters** like `num_workers`, `search_branching`, or `fill_tightened_domains_in_response`. Instead, his guidance focuses on a higher-level algorithmic strategy: partitioning the solution space across parallel workers by fixing subsets of variables, rather than relying solely on built-in solver parallelism for exhaustive enumeration."}]},"uuid":"25dcc542-6189-4392-b734-547e297b534c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:04.750Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4586d40f-cafa-48a2-b9e9-f685d7010de8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"25dcc542-6189-4392-b734-547e297b534c","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a21c8156ce15501b0","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01NED9njzwHcBEJGcV6Z3cxm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013NvdfCyQ122mZNJasDvBK7","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/_UOHuLu7Nws","prompt":"Extract the discussion about forcing CP-SAT to use specific subsolvers. List the subsolver names mentioned, the exact_subsolvers / extra_subsolvers / ignore_subsolvers / subsolvers parameters, and any direct quote from Laurent Perron or core maintainers."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1146,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2233,"cache_read_input_tokens":32361,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2233,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":51,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaosNWcaHBKTmgYzK351i","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"965def83-dfc6-4916-814d-af689238d355","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:04.823Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"965def83-dfc6-4916-814d-af689238d355","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a21c8156ce15501b0","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01NED9njzwHcBEJGcV6Z3cxm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Tu29f88iQSC5VxLEiZ9wTj","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/pQ4B7QD6ebw","prompt":"Extract the discussion about CP-SAT custom combination of subsolvers. List subsolver names, parameter blocks (subsolver_params), and direct quotes from Laurent Perron."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1146,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2233,"cache_read_input_tokens":32361,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2233,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":51,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaosNWcaHBKTmgYzK351i","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"49745e45-e01e-4dc0-bb7c-b40898a56462","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:06.592Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"7c5eabe9-c54e-4abc-b1a3-2a5ad111da2e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a21c8156ce15501b0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XKZoE6AxozWCdRw1MAZyx9","type":"tool_result","content":"# Laurent Perron's Advice for Large CP-SAT Models\n\n## Initial Diagnostic Steps\n\nWhen a solver appears to complete without solving, Laurent recommends enabling logging: **\"add solver.parameters.log_search_progress = True\"** to identify if the problem is infeasible.\n\n## Debugging Infeasible Models\n\nFor models that are found infeasible, Laurent suggests exporting the model and analyzing it:\n\n1. **Export the model** using `model.ExportToFile(...)`\n2. **Run the sat_runner binary** with detailed parameters to trace where infeasibility occurs during preprocessing\n\n## Key Technical Limitation\n\nAn important constraint exists in CP-SAT: **\"There is a 2gb limit on proto size (internal size).\"** This becomes critical for very large models, as the internal representation may exceed memory constraints even if the raw file is smaller.\n\n## Practical Recommendation\n\nWhen encountering segmentation faults with large models, Joshua Friedman (following Laurent's guidance) suggests **\"increasing swap space\"** as a potential workaround for memory-intensive problems."}]},"uuid":"ac82dab7-1626-4358-a6f2-e1e464fd56bf","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:08.137Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7c5eabe9-c54e-4abc-b1a3-2a5ad111da2e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"965def83-dfc6-4916-814d-af689238d355","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a21c8156ce15501b0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013NvdfCyQ122mZNJasDvBK7","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP-SAT Subsolver Configuration Discussion\n\n## Subsolver Names Mentioned\n\n**Full problem subsolvers:** core, default_lp, lb_tree_search, max_lp, no_lp, objective_lb_search, probing, pseudo_costs, quick_restart, quick_restart_no_lp, reduced_costs\n\n**First solution subsolvers:** fj_long_default, fj_short_default, fs_random, fs_random_quick_restart\n\n**Incomplete/improvement subsolvers:** feasibility_pump, graph_arc_lns, graph_cst_lns, graph_dec_lns, graph_var_lns, rins/rens, rnd_cst_lns, rnd_var_lns, routing_full_path_lns, routing_path_lns, routing_random_lns, violation_ls\n\n## Configuration Parameters\n\nLaurent Perron identified three parameter options for controlling subsolvers:\n- `subsolvers` (clean replacement)\n- `extra_subsolvers`\n- `ignore_subsolvers`\n\n## Key Quote from Laurent Perron\n\n\"The first solution solvers die after the first feasible solution is found. The improvement solvers start after the first feasible solution is found.\"\n\nAdditionally, he cautioned: \"removing a subsolver that has zero visible effect is sometimes not a good idea\" due to hidden collaborative benefits between subsolvers."}]},"uuid":"494d4120-38b4-4a83-a67c-ee62f6efe1cb","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:09.465Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"965def83-dfc6-4916-814d-af689238d355","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"49745e45-e01e-4dc0-bb7c-b40898a56462","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a21c8156ce15501b0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Tu29f88iQSC5VxLEiZ9wTj","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP-SAT Subsolvers Discussion Summary\n\n## Subsolver Names\n\nAccording to Laurent Perron's response, CP-SAT uses the following subsolvers:\n\n**Complete solvers:** default_lp, fixed, pseudo_costs, no_lp, max_lp, and core\n\n**Additional workers that cycle:** LNS variants (rnd_var_lns_default, rnd_cst_lns_default, graph_var_lns_default, graph_cst_lns_default, scheduling_time_window_lns_default, scheduling_random_lns_default, rins_lns_default, rens_lns_default), feasibility_pump, quick_restart, quick_restart_no_lp, probing, and lb_tree_search\n\n## Key Parameters Mentioned\n\n- `num_search_workers` - Controls number of parallel workers\n- `optimize_with_core` - Enables core-based solving\n- `optimize_with_max_hs` - Parameter existence questioned by Laurent\n- `search_branching` - Set to FIXED_SEARCH in Mark's case\n\n## Direct Quote from Laurent Perron\n\n\"Fixed will only be included if a search strategy is defined. Core will only be included if the objective is a sum.\"\n\nHe also noted: \"The rest of the workers will cycle across the remaining lns + feasibility pump.\"\n\n## Key Finding\n\nLaurent indicated that \"no_lp and fixed_search are mostly deterministic,\" making custom worker allocation impractical for Mark's initial question about allocating 4 cores to each subsolver type."}]},"uuid":"fc9ed1a6-ead2-4adc-99f7-ade56c57d5f6","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:12.561Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"49745e45-e01e-4dc0-bb7c-b40898a56462","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
