{"parentUuid":"3ef913e1-a976-4c10-b3a3-1741d6ddcfee","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a21c8156ce15501b0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013FLYm74YsT3JLKRTdk2edG","type":"tool_result","content":"# Laurent Perron's CP-SAT Monitoring Recommendations\n\nBased on the discussion thread, Laurent Perron explicitly stated that **direct search monitoring is unavailable** for CP-SAT:\n\n> \"It is not available. Search is very different in a sat solver.\"\n\n## Performance Analysis Approach\n\nRather than real-time monitoring, Perron recommended a benchmarking methodology:\n\n- Generate multiple models that complete within reasonable timeframes\n- Collect metrics: running time and number of conflicts across instances\n- Compare models systematically across datasets\n- Note that \"There is too much luck in search to conclude from 1 example\"\n\n## Key Technical Insight\n\nPerron identified a critical difference in solver behavior: the CP-SAT solver embeds a simplex algorithm that processes linear equations from constraint models but does not receive interval variable information. He noted this linear relaxation capability guides search performance—models with explicit equations receive better propagation than those relying solely on interval variables without accompanying constraints.\n\n**No specific logging parameters, callbacks, or detailed monitoring tools were mentioned** as alternatives in this conversation."}]},"uuid":"b9c9a771-9181-4b9f-98cd-335a4a2640e9","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:24.255Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3ef913e1-a976-4c10-b3a3-1741d6ddcfee","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"06ab6ec7-6985-4f36-81c6-f835a6a3cdf8","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a21c8156ce15501b0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014u1boiLMgrkn34TewHWQp9","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT \"shared_tree_num_workers\" \"shared_tree\" parameter Laurent recommendation 2024 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"Parallel search problem in CP-SAT solver\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/i3TF_Szuz_k\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT claims to find optimal solution to a MILP\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/4fcAuWiIUFA\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"The CP-SAT-LP Solver Laurent Perron # Google, Paris, France Frédéric Didier #\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol280-cp2023/LIPIcs.CP.2023.3/LIPIcs.CP.2023.3.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT solver couldn't prove the solution is optimal if num_workers < 5 but otherwise it did instantly. · Issue #3662 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3662\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT produces nondeterministic results · Issue #3590 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3590\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT for scheduling Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://schedulingseminar.com/presentations/SchedulingSeminar_LaurentPerron.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I was not able to find specific information about the CP-SAT `shared_tree_num_workers` or `shared_tree` parameter with recommendations from Laurent Perron for 2024-2025. \n\nThe search returned results related to CP-SAT in general, including documents and discussions by Laurent Perron (who is a lead developer of CP-SAT at Google), but none of the results contained specific details about the `shared_tree_num_workers` parameter or its recommended settings.\n\nTo find more detailed information about this specific parameter and any recent recommendations, you might want to:\n1. Check the official OR-Tools GitHub repository and issues\n2. Look at the CP-SAT solver's parameter documentation directly\n3. Search the OR-Tools discussion forums for more recent discussions about this parameter\n\nWould you like me to perform additional searches with different queries to find this information?\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"12add91c-35db-46d3-ad73-9c282fead315","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:27.399Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"06ab6ec7-6985-4f36-81c6-f835a6a3cdf8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"00367852-b799-4742-86b8-1181ce1e16b8","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a21c8156ce15501b0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UELu4emX4Jxojq7Pms4LVC","type":"tool_result","content":"# Recently Added CP-SAT Parameters (2024-2026)\n\nBased on the proto file content, here are notable recent parameters:\n\n## Parallel Workers & Scheduling\n- **`num_full_subsolvers`** (default: 0): Controls how many subsolvers consume full threads versus interleaved ones\n- **`interleave_search`** (default: false): Experimental feature distributing major search strategies across workers deterministically\n- **`max_num_deterministic_batches`** (default: 0): Limits scheduled batches when interleaving is enabled\n\n## Proof & Verification (New)\n- **`check_lrat_proof`** (default: false): Validates inferred clauses using LRAT checking\n- **`output_lrat_proof`** (default: false): Exports LRAT proofs across presolve and workers\n- **`check_drat_proof`** (default: false): Verifies UNSAT via DRAT proof\n- **`check_merged_lrat_proof`** (default: false): Validates merged proof correctness\n\n## Presolve Enhancements\n- **`find_clauses_that_are_exactly_one`** (default: true): Detects clauses promotable to exactly-one constraints\n- **`load_at_most_ones_in_sat_presolve`** (default: false): Incorporates at-most-one constraints into SAT presolve\n- **`remove_fixed_variables_early`** (default: true): \"Remap all the model to a dense set of variable\" after initial fixing\n\n## Inprocessing Features\n- **`inprocessing_use_congruence_closure`** (default: true): Applies clausal congruence closure algorithm\n- **`inprocessing_use_sat_sweeping`** (default: false): Experimental SAT sweeping technique\n\n## Subsolver Management\n- **`filter_subsolvers`** & **`ignore_subsolvers`**: Glob-pattern filtering for subsolver selection"}]},"uuid":"537604d9-54a0-416a-aef9-35d59822acad","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:28.392Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"00367852-b799-4742-86b8-1181ce1e16b8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
